.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead dep" 1  "bead dep " 
.SH NAME
bead dep \- Manage dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead dep\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add or remove dependency edges between issues.
.PP
An edge is written blocked\-first: `bead dep add <BLOCKED> <BLOCKER>` means
BLOCKER must close before BLOCKED can become ready. `blocks` edges affect the
ready frontier and may not form cycles; `relates_to` edges are informational
only and may.
.PP
  bead dep add <BLOCKED> <BLOCKER> [\-\-kind blocks|relates_to]
  bead dep remove <BLOCKED> <BLOCKER> [\-\-kind KIND]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
bead dep\-add(1)
Add a dependency edge
.TP
bead dep\-remove(1)
Remove a dependency edge
.TP
bead dep\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
